<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Ngọc Hồi–Đống Đa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1789</span> · Also known as Battle of Dong Da, Battle of Đống Đa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Ngọc Hồi–Đống Đa was fought around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thang-long">Thăng Long</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanoi">Hanoi</a>) in early 1789, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quang-trung">Nguyen Hue</a>, who had just proclaimed himself Emperor Quang Trung, launched a surprise Lunar New Year attack on a Qing army sent to restore the Later Le dynasty. The Qing forces were routed, the last Le emperor fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, and the Tay Son secured northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>.</p></div>
